# SOS App - AI Assistant Guidelines

## Project Overview
- **Project Name**: SOSApp
- **Type**: React Native mobile application built with Expo
- **Target Platforms**: iOS and Android mobile devices
- **Purpose**: Emergency alert application that allows users to send pre-configured emergency alerts to specified recipients
- **Repository**: https://github.com/Mgonzalez-droid/SOSApp

### App Functionality
SOSApp is an emergency alert system designed for modern smartphones. When activated, users can send emergency alerts containing configurable information:
- **Location Data**: GPS coordinates (with user permission)
- **Medical Information**: User-configured medical details (allergies, conditions, blood type, etc.)
- **Custom Message**: User-defined emergency message or alert text
- **Recipient List**: Pre-configured list of emergency contacts to receive alerts

### Future Features
Additional features are planned for future development phases and will be detailed in Jira tickets.

### Monetization
- **Strategy**: Google AdMob integration for mobile advertising revenue
- **Web**: No current plans for web-based version; focus is exclusively on native mobile

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Expo 54.0.21
- **Runtime**: React 19.1.0, React Native 0.81.5
- **Routing**: Expo Router v6.0.14 (file-based routing)
- **Language**: TypeScript 5.9.2
- **Platform Support**: iOS, Android (Web support may be added in future but not currently planned)
- **Linting**: ESLint with Expo config

